# === Cloudflare Pages example — local config, DO NOT COMMIT with your values ===
# Usage:
#   cp deploy-examples/cloudflare.example .deploy.local   (then fill in below)
#   npm run package                                        (build + ZIP)
#   npm run package:deploy                                 (build + ZIP + auto-upload, tokens required)
#
# Notes:
# - Normal deploy: Cloudflare dashboard > Pages > Connect to Git
#   (build: node scripts/build.mjs --target cloudflare, output: public).
# - Manual upload: Pages > project > Upload assets.
# - IP counter (single Worker+D1 backend, see IPS.md + workers/README.md):
#   `npx wrangler d1 create visits`, paste database_id into
#   workers/wrangler.visits.toml AND wrangler.toml, migrate workers/schema.sql,
#   deploy the Worker, then fill in HUGO_VISIT_API_URL below.

# Target platform (do not change in this file)
TARGET=cloudflare

# Final public URL — REQUIRED:
# https://mon-site.pages.dev  |  https://www.mon-domaine.fr
SITE_URL=https://mon-site.pages.dev

# --- Single visits/IP backend (optional, see IPS.md) ---
# HUGO_VISIT_API_URL=https://mon-licenciement-visits.<account>.workers.dev/api/visit

# --- SEO: verification + IndexNow (optional, see DEPLOY.md SEO section) ---
# HUGO_GOOGLE_SITE_VERIFICATION=
# HUGO_BING_SITE_VERIFICATION=
# INDEXNOW_KEY= (generate via npm run seo:init)

# --- Giscus comments (optional, see COMMENTAIRES.md) ---
# Uncomment and fill in the 4 values copied from https://giscus.app
# GISCUS_REPO=USER/REPO
# GISCUS_REPO_ID=R_xxx
# GISCUS_CATEGORY=Announcements
# GISCUS_CATEGORY_ID=DIC_xxx

# --- API tokens (required ONLY for `npm run package:deploy`) ---
# My Profile > API Tokens (Pages template) ; Account ID: dashboard, right column
# Pages project name as shown in the dashboard.
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
# CF_PROJECT=mon-site
